course: dictionary
lesson: 6507
title: Needless and needlessly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Needless» means not necessary. It describes something bad that did not have to happen, or something that could have been avoided. «Needless hurt» is hurt that nobody had to cause.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Free speech is precious, but so is not causing needless hurt to others.» The words «but so is» tell you that avoiding hurt matters just as much as free speech. Ask yourself: could this have been avoided? If yes, «needless» fits.
explain: Watch out for the phrase «needless to say». It does not mean nobody needs to say anything. It means «as you would expect», or «it is obvious». Someone might say «Needless to say, the match was cancelled in the rain» when they think you already know the answer.
fact: Needless means not necessary.
fact: «Needless hurt» means hurt that did not have to happen.
fact: Needlessly is the adverb: «needlessly cruel» means cruel when there was no need to be.
fact: «Needless to say» means «as you would expect» or «it is obvious».
fact: When you see needless, look for a warning: something bad could have been avoided.
exercise: «Disagreeing with someone's religion is fine; mocking what they hold holy causes needless hurt.» What does needless hurt mean? | *Hurt that did not have to happen | Hurt that makes everyone happy | Hurt that a teacher asked for | Hurt that is very large and must be done
exercise: In «needlessly cruel», what does needlessly mean? | Very slowly | With great care and love | Only sometimes | *Without any need, when it did not have to be
exercise: Which phrase means «as you would expect»? | Needlessly cruel | Needless risk | *Needless to say | Needless waste
test: Someone says «Needless to say, we were late.» What does it mean here? | *It was obvious we would be late | We were not late at all | We did not have to be late | We were needed at school
test: Which sentence shows needless waste? | We put the rubbish in the bin | We turned the lights off when we left the room | We planted a tree in the park | *We left the tap running all night for no reason
exam: Which word means the same as needless in «needless hurt»? | Helpful | *Unnecessary | Loud | Kind
